19934860,2026-03-03,Debt collection,Telecommunications debt,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt is not yours,"I am filing this complaint against Jefferson Capital Systems , LLC for reporting and attempting to collect an alleged XXXX XXXX debt that I formally disputed. 

On XX/XX/XXXX, I sent a certified debt validation request and notice of dispute to the company. The certified mail receipt confirms delivery and signature. In my letter, I requested the original signed contract, full itemized accounting, proof of assignment/chain of title from XXXX, and proof that the company is licensed to collect debt in the State of Florida. 

Jefferson Capital Systems , LLC failed to respond and failed to provide any validation. 

Despite receiving my dispute, the company continues to report this account to the credit bureaus. The account is being reported with an incorrect open date of XX/XX/XXXX, which is impossible and materially misleading. This inaccurate reporting appears to be an attempt to re-age the debt and violates the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA 623 ).

Additionally, based on my research through regulatory databases, Jefferson Capital Systems , LLC does not appear to hold a valid Florida collection agency license. Collecting or attempting to collect consumer debt in Florida without proper licensure violates Florida Statute 559.553.

The company has ignored my certified dispute, failed to validate the debt, and continues to report inaccurate information. I am requesting immediate deletion of this account from all credit reporting agencies and confirmation that collection activity has ceased.",,CL Holdings LLC,FL,326XX,,Web,2026-03-03,Closed with explanation,Yes
