20208599,2026-03-12,Checking or savings account,CD (Certificate of Deposit),Managing an account,Deposits or withdrawals,"Complaint Against Synchrony Bank IRA CD Early Withdrawal Penalties I am submitting this complaint regarding early withdrawal penalties charged by Synchrony Bank in connection with withdrawals from XXXX of my IRA CDs. 



Before initiating the transaction on XX/XX/year>,, I called Synchrony Bank and asked a very specific question : whether I could withdraw any amount at any time for any reason. The representative informed me that I could, explaining that this was because I had reached the age at which Required Minimum Distributions apply. At no point during that call was I informed that withdrawing funds from the IRA CDs would result in substantial early withdrawal penalties. 



Relying on that information, I proceeded with the transaction. Synchrony Bank subsequently charged early withdrawal penalties of {$1400.00} on XXXX IRA XXXX and {$1700.00} on another IRA CD, for a total of {$3100.00}. 



If I had been informed that penalties of this magnitude would apply, I would not have proceeded with the transaction at that time. 



I escalated this matter internally with Synchrony Bank, including to their Executive Response Team. I was informed that the call recording had been reviewed. Synchrony Banks explanation for refusing to reverse the penalties was that the transaction was not a withdrawal but rather a trustee-to-trustee transfer, and that because I did not take possession of the funds, the penalty was required. 



However, my understanding is that trustee-to-trustee transfer rules relate to tax treatment under Internal Revenue Service regulations and do not require a bank to impose a CD early withdrawal penalty. Early withdrawal penalties arise from the contractual terms of the CD, not from federal law governing IRA transfers. 



The central issue is that I specifically contacted Synchrony Bank in advance to ask whether I could withdraw funds, and the representative informed me that I could because I had reached the age where Required Minimum Distributions apply. The substantial early withdrawal penalties totaling {$3100.00} were not disclosed during that conversation. 



Because I relied on the information provided by Synchrony Banks representative when making my decision, I believe the penalties were applied based on incomplete or misleading information. 



Resolution Requested : I respectfully request a full refund of the {$3100.00} in early withdrawal penalties. 



Because this matter involves what was disclosed during my phone call, I also request that Synchrony Bank provide the call recording or documentation showing that the early withdrawal penalties were clearly disclosed to me when I asked about withdrawing funds. 



I also request that Synchrony Bank preserve the recording of that call and all related records while this matter remains under formal dispute. 

Sent from my XXXX",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL,FL,33487,"Older American, Servicemember",Web,2026-03-12,Closed with explanation,Yes
