20480741,2026-03-21,Debt collection,Telecommunications debt,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt was paid,"I am filing this complaint against Waypoint Resource Group LLC for inaccurate and duplicate debt reporting in violation of the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ) and the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ). 

The original creditor is XXXX XXXX. That debt was placed with XXXX XXXX XXXX, and subsequently assigned to XXXX XXXX XXXX I have logged into XXXX XXXX 's portal and established a formal payment arrangement, with my first scheduled payment on XX/XX/year>. 

I recently reviewed my credit report and discovered that Waypoint Resource Group LLC is separately reporting this same XXXX XXXX  debt as an outstanding unpaid collection. I have never been contacted by Waypoint Resource Group LLC, never received written notice that my debt was transferred or sold to them, and have no account number or reference number associated with them. I was given no opportunity to validate or dispute this debt before it appeared on my credit report. 

This is a violation of my rights for the following reasons : 1. DUPLICATE REPORTING The same original XXXX XXXX  debt is being reported by two separate collection agencies simultaneously ( XXXX XXXX and Waypoint Resource Group LLC ). I have an active, scheduled payment arrangement with XXXX XXXX to resolve this obligation, yet Waypoint Resource Group LLC is reporting the same debt as a separate unpaid balance. This is inaccurate and materially damaging to my credit. 

2. NO NOTICE OF TRANSFER Under the FDCPA ( 15 U.S.C. 1692g ), I am entitled to written notice of any debt being collected against me, including who owns it and the amount owed. I received no such notice from Waypoint Resource Group LLC at any time. 

3. CREDIT DAMAGE The duplicate reporting has significantly and negatively impacted my credit score, affecting my ability to access credit and financial products. 

I am requesting that the CFPB investigate Waypoint Resource Group LLC and require them to immediately remove this inaccurate duplicate entry from all credit bureaus. I also request clarification on the current legal owner of this debt to ensure my XXXX payments are being properly applied and that I am not at risk of unknowingly paying two parties for the same obligation. 

I have not contacted Waypoint Resource Group LLC directly out of concern that doing so could be misconstrued as acknowledgment of a separate debt obligation. I am seeking CFPB intervention to resolve this matter.",,"Waypoint Resource Group, LLC",OR,97420,,Web,2026-04-16,Closed with explanation,Yes
