 ) to POOR ( XXXX ). This credit score decrease has prohibited my ability to close on my new home loan at a lower rate with an alternative mortgage lender and to apply for new personal credit. My newly decreased credit score has harmed my business credit, as my personal credit was used to guarantee my business credit, occasioning card closures. Shellpoint was previously found guilty by your organization of charging my loan with an unnecessary homeowner 's insurance policy for over {$4000.00} in full knowledge of my possession of an active policy. I did not apply for a loan with Shellpoint. Shellpoint bought my loan from the original lender. Shellpoint has also harmed another member of my church, who was forced to declare bankruptcy from similar practices. In both instances, my friend and I were counseled 1 ) not to make payments until the deferment process was reviewed, 2 ) to "" trust the process '' despite questioning multiple changes of staff, and 3 ) to allow for processing delays of 30-90 days, sustaining harmful credit score decreases. Shellpoint, in two separate instances, has made it a business practice of delaying processing of deferments to force homeownwers into losing their properties by default or filing bankruptcy to save their homes. In either event, protections should be placed for homeowners against Shellpoint 's tactics aimed disproportionately to harm minority homeowners.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"Shellpoint Partners, LLC",AL,36526,,Web,2026-04-16,Closed with explanation,Yes
