My Position : I refuse to be a participant in these predatory lending tactics. Effective immediately, I have closed this account. 

I am willing to pay the legitimate debt incurred for the goods purchased. I have enclosed a check ( or made a payment online ) for {$53.00}, which covers the principal balance in full. 

I explicitly refuse to pay the {$42.00} in fees. I consider the principal balance satisfied and the account closed. 

Regarding Credit Reporting : Do not report this account as "" delinquent '' or "" charged off '' to the credit bureaus ( XXXX XXXX XXXX ). The principal debt has been paid. Reporting negative information regarding these disputed, predatory fees will be considered a violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ). If you report a negative mark based on these disputed fees, I will pursue all available remedies, including filing complaints with the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ) and state Attorney General. 

Resolution : Please adjust the account balance to XXXX, waive the {$42.00} in contested fees, and send me a written confirmation that the account is closed with a "" Paid as Agreed '' status. 

This is the second letter : Comenity Capital Bank Attn : Billing Errors/ Dispute Department XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX XXXXXXXX Subject : SECOND NOTICE OF DISPUTE - Escalation Regarding Predatory Compounding Fees Account Number : XXXX Previous Correspondence Date : XXXX To the Dispute Department : I am writing to formally escalate my ongoing dispute regarding my closed XXXX XXXX account XXXX 

