20764316,2026-03-30,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Opening an account,Didn't receive terms that were advertised,"I am filing this complaint against SoFi Bank regarding a direct deposit welcome bonus promotion that I believe was administered unfairly and without adequate disclosure. 

I opened a SoFi checking account and was offered a {$50.00} bonus for receiving {$1000.00} or more in direct deposits within a 25-day eligibility window ( XX/XX/XXXX through XX/XX/year> ). I made multiple deposits during this period totaling well over {$1000.00}. SoFi has since informed me that I received only {$990.00} in qualifying direct deposits, {$3.00} short of the threshold, because they excluded certain deposits from their count. 

Specifically, SoFi excluded deposits I received from XXXX and from my Found business account. These are legitimate ACH deposits from established financial platforms, and nothing in SoFi 's promotional terms indicated that deposits from these sources would be disqualified. I was not informed that SoFi would apply its own internal classification system to determine which deposits counted, nor was I given any opportunity to substitute qualifying deposits during the eligibility period. 

Had SoFi clearly defined what types of deposits would and would not qualify, I could have adjusted my behavior accordingly. Instead, I acted in good faith, met what I reasonably understood to be the requirements, and was denied the bonus on a {$3.00} technicality created entirely by SoFi 's undisclosed eligibility criteria. 

I contacted SoFi directly and requested that they honor the {$50.00} bonus as a courtesy given the circumstances. They refused. 

This is exactly the type of deceptive or misleading promotional practice the CFPB exists to address. A bank should not be permitted to advertise a bonus, apply opaque deposit classification criteria that are not clearly disclosed to consumers, and then deny a {$50.00} bonus based on a {$3.00} gap caused by their own vague terms. 

I am requesting that SoFi pay me the {$50.00} promotional bonus I earned in good faith. I am also requesting that the CFPB review SoFi 's direct deposit promotion practices to determine whether other consumers have been similarly affected by undisclosed deposit classification criteria.",,"SOFI TECHNOLOGIES, INC.",TX,XXXXX,,Web,2026-03-30,Closed with explanation,Yes
